## {#sigma-instructor data-menu-title="Worked Exercises" .smaller}

[Solutions]{.slide-title}

<hr>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="50%"}
**1)** 

$$\begin{align} \sum_{i=3}^6 3i &= (3\cdot 3) + (3\cdot 4) + (3 \cdot 5) + (3 \cdot 6)  \\
  &= 3(3 + 4 + 5 +6) \\
  &= 54
\end{align}
$$

:::


::: {.column width="50%"}
**2)** 

$$
\begin{align}
\sum_{i=2}^{5}(i^2-1) &= (4-1)+(9-1)+(16-1)+(25-1)\\
                        &= 3+8+15+24\\
                        &= 50
\end{align}
$$

:::

:::


**3)**

$$x_1 + x_2^2 + \cdots + x_n^n = \sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i^i$$


**4)** The formula is $\text{MSE} = \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\hat{y}_i - y_i)^2$. Compute each squared error first:

$$
\begin{align}
(\hat{y}_1 - y_1)^2 &= (22-24)^2 = 4\\
(\hat{y}_2 - y_2)^2 &= (25-23)^2 = 4\\
(\hat{y}_3 - y_3)^2 &= (20-21)^2 = 1
\end{align}
$$

Then apply the formula:

$$MSE = \frac{4+4+1}{3} = 3 \text{ °C}$$

