## {#dot-product data-menu-title="Dot product"}

[Dot product]{.slide-title}

<hr>

::: {.body-text-l}
For vectors 

$$x = (x_1, \ldots, x_n) \text{ and } y = (y_1, \ldots, y_n)$$ 

their **dot product** is:

$$x \cdot y = \sum_{i=1}^n x_i y_i$$
:::


[[**In words:**]{.body-text-m} The dot product is the sum of coordinates of each vector multiplied together. It is a measure of how close the vectors "point" in the same direction]{.body-text}

